From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:06:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Runner: a relay client that closes frames in lockstep
 (phase 1 prototype)

SR-Source Net Plus, phase 1. With SRNP_RELAY=<host>:<port>, SRNP_SEAT and
SRNP_SEATS, the runner joins a relay (tools/srnp/relais.py of the fork):
after every present, on the emulation thread, it sends its input for the
frame SRNP_DELAY (2) frames ahead and waits for the next frame's official
inputs, then hands seat k's input to the emulated pad of port k through
Dolphin's input overrider, so every runner reads the same inputs at the
same emulated moment. Every SRNP_CHECK (60) frames it sends an FNV-1a
hash of Sonic Riders' _Main.rel BSS, which the relay compares.
SRNP_INPUT=random:<seed> gives reproducible test inputs (no real pad
yet); SRNP_TRACE=1 traces the first frames. Text protocol, blocking TCP
(winsock on Windows). Nothing changes without SRNP_RELAY.

Four runners on one PC, the demo race's save state, native core: the
same MEM1 bit for bit at the pause and equal checksums; a runner at half
speed does not slow the three others down. Two JIT64 runners: the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
